# High-Contrast Dark Mode Redesign (V2)

Based on your feedback that the previous implementation was ugly, we will rebuild the dark mode entirely from scratch, strictly following your expert UI/UX and accessibility guidelines. We will abandon the colorful gradients and instead focus on a clean, professional, eye-strain-reduced aesthetic.

## Proposed Color System & Elevation Layers

We will implement a precise Tailwind CSS custom variable configuration mapping to these exact hex values:

1.  **Base Layer (Backgrounds):** Deep Charcoal / Slate (`#0f172a` - Tailwind `slate-900`). This completely avoids pure black `#000000` to prevent motion blur and harsh contrast.
2.  **Surface/Card Layer:** Raised Slate (`#1e293b` - Tailwind `slate-800`). Used for GlassCards and main content areas to create a clear visual hierarchy without relying on harsh borders.
3.  **Raised/Hover Layer:** Lighter Slate (`#334155` - Tailwind `slate-700`). Used for dropdowns, active states, and hover effects.
4.  **Borders & Dividers:** Subtle Slate (`#334155` - Tailwind `slate-700`).

## Typography & Contrast (WCAG AA)

We will avoid pure low-opacity white.
1.  **Primary Text (Body & Headers):** Cool Off-White (`#f1f5f9` - Tailwind `slate-100`). Ensures a minimum 4.5:1 contrast ratio against the `#0f172a` base without the halation effect of pure `#ffffff`.
2.  **Muted/Secondary Text:** Cool Gray (`#94a3b8` - Tailwind `slate-400`). Ensures readability for metadata and labels while clearly establishing a visual hierarchy.

## Interactive Elements & Accents

1.  **Brand Accents:** We will keep the primary brand Orange (`#E86C45`) as it inherently pops against deep slate backgrounds. 
2.  **Interactive States:** We will implement clear focus rings and hover states using the Raised Layer (`#334155`) so interactions are tactile and obvious.

